    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nIn the command-line window, nvim does not seem to properly treat characters that contain `\\x80`:\n\n- from ` ` (U+2000, `0xE2 0x80 0x80`) to `⁀` (U+2040, `0xE2 0x81 0x80`)\n- `₀` (U+2080, `0xE2 0x82 0x80`)\n- `℀` (U+2100, `0xE2 0x84 0x80`)\n\nThis bisects to b2bf7bcfb15125fe65f3e503af00174f31eb92d8 (#40325).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\ne.g. `…` (U+2026, `0xE2 0x80 0xA6`):\n\n```\nLANG=C.UTF-8 nvim --clean -c $'call histadd(\"/\", \"\\u2026\")'\nq/k<CR>\n\" does not search …\n<CR>\n\" /â\n<CR>\n\" E486: Pattern not found: â\n```\n\n<img width=\"559\" height=\"426\" alt=\"q/…\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/94566e94-edee-4028-8642-2a19f39247f6\" />\n\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`q/k<CR>` immediately searches `…`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n82ea5a8aac40331579113b961b6cef88865ad5a9\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2.1011\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
