            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "```diff\n--- a/runtime/lua/vim/_core/cmdwin.lua\n+++ b/runtime/lua/vim/_core/cmdwin.lua\n@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ function M.confirm()\n   end\n   local line, type = _close()\n   line = line:gsub('%z', '\\n'):gsub('(%c)', '\\022%1') -- Escape control characters.\n-  vim.api.nvim_feedkeys(type .. line .. vim.keycode('<CR>'), 'nt', false)\n+  vim.api.nvim_feedkeys(type .. line .. vim.keycode('<CR>'), 'nt', true)\n end\n```\nSeems to fix the issue and handle the input without resulting in other tests failing\n\n but I was unable to write a regression test as the editor was blocking for input and the failing version hanged, here was my attempt\n\n```diff\n--- a/test/functional/editor/cmdwin_spec.lua\n+++ b/test/functional/editor/cmdwin_spec.lua\n@@ -138,6 +138,12 @@ describe('cmdwin', function()\n     eq({ 'foo', 'bar' }, api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, 0, -1, false))\n   end)\n \n+  it('Handles Unicode characters that contain 0x80 #41558', function()\n+     fn.histadd('/', '\\u{2026}')\n+     feed('q/k<CR>')\n+     eq('', fn.getcmdwintype())\n+   end)\n+\n   it('async API calls work while cmdwin is open #40312', function()\n     feed('q:')\n     eq(':', fn.getcmdwintype())\n```\nIt passses on applying the patch but gets stuck in the failure scenario",
