        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Echoing my reply on Matrix in case it's missed, this should work:\n\n```lua\n  it('handles Unicode characters containing 0x80 #41558', function()\n    fn.histadd('/', '…')\n    feed('q/')\n    eq('/', fn.getcmdwintype())\n    feed('k<CR>')\n    eq(false, api.nvim_get_mode().blocking)\n    eq('', fn.getcmdwintype())\n    eq('E486: Pattern not found: …', api.nvim_get_vvar('errmsg'))\n  end)\n```\n\n(Also, avoid `\\u{...}` in tests; that's a LuaJIT extension from 5.3)",
